# Build context: ./backend
#
# What the image needs is go.mod and the source tree. Everything listed here
# either cannot work inside the image or only serves to invalidate the layer
# cache when it changes.

# Recipe and context filter: read by the daemon before the build, never copied.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Host binary from `go build -o server ./cmd/server`. Compiled for darwin/arm64
# and useless in a linux container, which is why the image builds its own.
server

# Coverage report. The numbers ship in the README, the artefact does not.
coverage.out

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# The _test.go files stay in the context on purpose: they cost kilobytes and
# they are what lets the Dockerfile keep a stage that runs `go test ./...`
# before the binary is built.
